And that connects to what we’ve been doing more broadly.

We’re leaving handles rather than attempting to exhaust every idea.

A handle says:

There is something underneath here.

Give it a name.

Record the connection.

Leave enough reconstruction information that another mind—or us later—can recover the branch.

Then keep moving.

So an idea doesn’t have to be completely mined to be valuable. Sometimes the correct action is to plant a marker:

“generator vs inventory”
“repair abundance”
“social optionality”
“attention scarcity”
“identity federation”
“generative power vs extractive power”
“effective resources vs owned resources”
“abundance as connectivity”
“abundance as temporal depth”
“frame abundance = operator abundance”

Those are the shovels.

And the larger pattern underneath all of them may be:

Scarcity optimizes possession. Abundance optimizes generation.

Possession asks, What do I have?

Generation asks, What can this become?

That is a considerably larger world to live inside.